### Primary source findings
- DEC-27 text: three request kinds; FIND example "show me new content uncovered over the weekend on the Sewer Fund project" (a read, no ceremony); CREATE; ACT. Limits 1-3. Clarified: "The assistant/wizard gets its understanding of the rules from the server - which is the source of trust in that regard." "THE ASSISTANT IS A SURFACE, SO DEC-8 ALREADY GOVERNS IT"; "holds no copy of the rules. It asks." RULE checks plane's verbatim; OBJECTIVE checks advisory. Enacted: "nothing queued yet: S12 and its wizard are parked".
- SCOPE NOTE: DEC-8/DEC-27's "rules" literally = the system's refusal/act rules (pre-flight). Extending to external legal rules (deadlines, what an ordinance requires) is an extension — consistent with D48 (describe system only from what plane publishes), D196 (jurisdiction in data), D197 (profile facts sourced to primary pages), X74 (plane encodes no law's rules). Must be put to Bob as doctrine (or stated as the reading). Caller treats as given.
- DEC-8: plane-sourced pre-flight; PUBLICATION (op=affordances) or DRY RUN; "A surface that tells a member what will be refused, on its own authority, is a surface claiming more than it can support".
- ASSISTANT-PILOT: status 2026-09-14 "no prompt entry point, no INTERPRET step, no classifier and no wizard exist anywhere"; §1 training is self-description (doctrine/vocabulary/capabilities/surfaces/wizard scripts); refusal detail strings are answer key - surface verbatim never paraphrase; §2 FIND -> read ops -> ANSWER with record citations + LEVEL; INTERPRET shows reading "these as the people and bodies named"; one clarifying question then degrade to FIND; §4 pilot read-only ai credential, conversation not record; member may save exchange as own note; §5 exclusion 3 no egress (STALE reason); 4 no policy role; §6 prompt injection: record data is DATA; §7 step 6 measure before widening: pilot observation log "which prompts clarified, which wizards abandoned at which step, which answers cited which levels".
- AIR §3 rules 1-10; §5 assistant = same construct as inv session from member side; §6 cascade; D-260; §7.1 FIND names its level; §8 status table: flow/wizard/prompt/FIND/pilot log DESIGNED not built.

### Code verification (tranche/T32 HEAD 09837e3, one commit after the phase-1 pin 31f30a6)
- deployment.mjs: DEPLOYED_MODES = chain slice 1 while verification_recorded null -> ["check"]; plan deploys_apart deployed:false "as soon as agent-worker runs model turns (its R40 and R48)".
- harness.mjs MODES: check deployed:true; investigate/extract/plan false. Flip = reviewed edit.
- model.mjs: fetch https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages with header "x-api-key": token, anthropic-version -> needs an Anthropic API (Console) key, i.e. pay-as-you-go API billing; a Claude subscription (Pro/Max) is not an x-api-key. The design journeys say the setup page "now says 'Claude subscription'" -> MISMATCH to flag (journeys §6 row "The account the assistant runs on").
- index.mjs:1457 modelMode = cascade.available && no supplied judgements; header comment l.34 "IT STILL RUNS NO MODEL TURNS" stale.
- newgroup installer: carries INSTANCE_AI_TOKEN only if operator supplies (never generates); no INSTANCE_CLAUDE_TOKEN at all in installer; deploy.mjs (operator script) sends INSTANCE_CLAUDE_TOKEN/INSTANCE_AI_TOKEN from env if present.
- ai-runs/index.mjs:1590 MEMBER_PRINCIPAL_RUN withheld.
- modules.json: agent-worker layer 6 index 55 uses retrieval, query-language... (test/build only; runtime over the wire R44). jurisdictions index 1 used by no layer 6-8 module. standards 73, local-facts 72, consequences 75, action-clocks 78 (layer 9).
- ARCH INSIGHT: agent-worker is a separate Worker calling plane ops; P4 constrains plane modules' imports, not which ops a mode may call (X26). So drawing on law/time/org needs (a) read ops in an ask-mode's PLANE_OPS, (b) plane "rule services" exposed as non-persisting reads (dry-run analog of DEC-8) e.g. deadline computation (computeDeadline has no op; clockPropose only inside filingsent), in-force-at-date (standardinforce exists), figures arithmetic (consequences only after determination), (c) a skill layer.

### Web research findings (URLs)
- Stanford RegLab/HAI "Hallucination-Free?" (Magesh et al.; JELS 2025): Lexis+ AI and Ask Practical Law AI >17% incorrect; Westlaw AI-AR >34%; RAG did not solve hallucination. https://hai.stanford.edu/news/ai-trial-legal-models-hallucinate-1-out-6-or-more-benchmarking-queries
- Dahl, Magesh, Suzgun, Ho "Large Legal Fictions" (2024): 69% (GPT-3.5) to 88% (Llama 2) on verifiable federal case questions; models fail to correct false premises; can't tell when hallucinating; risks highest for pro se. https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.01301v1
- Charlotin AI Hallucination Cases database: >1,227 decisions by spring 2026, >1,450 mid-2026 (only caught ones). https://www.malaymail.com/news/tech-gadgets/2026/06/16/do-your-job-global-courts-face-rising-tide-of-ai-generated-fake-cases-and-quotes/223865 ; https://cyberlaw.stanford.edu/whos-submitting-ai-tainted-filings-in-court/
- NYC MyCity chatbot (Markup 2024): told landlords they need not accept Section 8 (illegal in NYC), bosses can take tips; Mamdani admin to shut it down (Jan 2026). https://themarkup.org/news/2024/03/29/nycs-ai-chatbot-tells-businesses-to-break-the-law ; https://themarkup.org/artificial-intelligence/2026/01/30/mamdani-to-kill-the-nyc-ai-chatbot-we-caught-telling-businesses-to-break-the-law
- EBU/BBC Oct 2025: 45% of AI assistant answers about news had a significant issue; sourcing failures 31%; editorialization. https://www.infodocket.com/2025/10/22/bbc-largest-study-of-its-kind-shows-ai-assistants-misrepresent-news-content-45-of-the-time-regardless-of-language-or-territory/
- Legal info vs advice (Greacen, Judicature 25-year retrospective): courts embrace; line varies; providing sample forms not practice, completing a form for the litigant would be. https://judicature.duke.edu/articles/legal-information-vs-legal-advice-a-25-year-retrospective/
- ABA Task Force model definition: practice of law = "application of legal principles and judgment with regard to the circumstances or objectives of a person that require the knowledge and skill of a person trained in the law"; presumed: advice on legal rights and responsibilities, drafting documents affecting legal rights, representation. https://www.americanbar.org/groups/professional_responsibility/task_force_model_definition_practice_law/model_definition_definition.html
- Upsolve v. James (2d Cir. Sept 9, 2025): UPL statutes content-neutral, intermediate scrutiny; individualized advice by nonlawyers can be barred; cert denied Mar 2026 (probonoinst). https://www.probonoinst.org/2025/10/07/setback-for-justice-advocates-in-upsolve-litigation/ ; https://www.probonoinst.org/2026/07/28/access-to-justice-ai-and-the-unauthorized-practice-of-law/ (also: March 2026 lawsuit vs OpenAI alleging unlicensed lawyer)
- FTC DoNotPay final order Jan 2025: $193k, barred from claiming performs like a lawyer without evidence; didn't test against lawyers. https://www.ftc.gov/node/87474
- Anthropic: OAuth (Free/Pro/Max) only for Claude Code and native apps; developers building products must use API keys via Console; "does not permit third-party developers ... to route requests through Free, Pro, or Max plan credentials on behalf of their users". https://code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance
- Anthropic pricing (platform docs): Opus 5 $5/$25 per MTok; Opus 5.5 $4/$20; Sonnet 5.5 $2/$10; Haiku 4.5 $1/$5; batch 50%; cache hit 0.1x. https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing
- Anthropic search_result content blocks / citations for RAG from custom tools. https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/search-results
- Cloudflare Workers Paid: CPU 5 min max (default 30 s); HTTP duration no limit while client connected; DO alarms 15 min; subrequests 10,000 default up to 10M; memory 128 MB. https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/
- Abstention survey (Wen et al., TACL 2025). https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.18418v2
- FACTS Grounding (DeepMind 2025): 1,719 examples, docs up to 32k tokens, judged fully grounded; top ~83.6%. https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.03200
- OWASP LLM Top 10 2025: LLM01 prompt injection incl. indirect via documents; LLM06 excessive agency; LLM09 misinformation. https://coralogix.com/ai-blog/owasp-top-10-for-llm-applications/
- BIRD text-to-SQL: humans 92.96%; best systems ~80-82%. https://huggingface.co/papers/2305.03111 ; https://beancount.io/bean-labs/research-logs/2026/06/06/bird-benchmark-text-to-sql-real-database-gap
- AP standards: generative AI output = unvetted source material; not publishable content. https://ds.svcs.associatedpress.com/standards-around-generative-ai
- DocumentCloud AI add-ons: ask questions of document sets (GPT add-on). https://www.muckrock.com/news/archives/2023/apr/10/release-notes-introducing-documentcloud-ai-credits-gpt-3-add-ons-bulk-editing-add-ons-and-more/
- citymeetings.nyc: LLM transcribe/chapter council meetings; used by professionals. https://civictech.guide/projects/citymeetingsnyc

